==Latin==
[[File:Ficus carica0.jpg|thumb|fīcī (figs)]]

===Etymology===
Potentially related to {{cog|grc|σῦκον}} and {{cog|xcl|թուզ}} via a Mediterranean {{der|la|qfa-sub|-}} form ''*θuiko-'' or the like.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|page=218|head=fīcus}}</ref>

One possibility is a {{bor|la|sem|-}} loanword. Compare {{cog|phn|𐤐𐤀𐤂||half-ripe fig}}, {{cog|he|פַּג|tr=paḡ}}, {{m|he|פַּגָּה|tr=paggâ|t=unripe fig}}, {{cog|syc|ܦܵܓܵܐ|t=unripe fig}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|fīcus}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|((fīcus<2>,fīcus<4>))|g=m|g2=f}}

# [[fig tree]]
# [[fig]] ([[fruit]])
# [[hemorrhoids]]

====Declension====
Even among Classical grammarians, the gender (masculine or feminine) and [[declension]] (second or fourth) were debated.
